{
    "background_story": "Alani was a proud descendant of the ancient Rajput warriors of India. Growing up in a small village in Rajasthan, she was regaled with stories of her ancestors' bravery and chivalry. Alani's parents, wanting to preserve their cultural heritage, trained her in the traditional arts of sword fighting and horse riding. As she grew older, Alani became an expert in the martial art of Gatka and a skilled horseback rider. She was particularly drawn to the legend of Rani Karnavati, the fearless queen who defended her kingdom against invaders. Inspired by her ancestor's courage, Alani joined the Indian Army and rose through the ranks, earning the respect of her comrades and superiors alike. Today, she is a proud symbol of Rajput valor and a role model for young women everywhere.",
